\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 ## Astoria Open: System Architecture Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
Astoria Open is an advanced Natural Language to SQL (NL2SQL) application designed to answer questions about a maritime database. It uses a multi-layered approach, combining fast rule-based systems with powerful Large Language Models (LLMs) to provide accurate, context-aware, and credible narrative answers.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 ### Core Components \uc0\u55358 \u56809 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Web Server (Flask)
\f0\b0 : The backbone of the application, running in 
\f2\b\fs26 main.py
\f0\b0\fs24 . It exposes a REST API that the user interface can communicate with.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Manual Override Router
\f0\b0 : The central logic in 
\f2\b\fs26 nl_query_service.py
\f0\b0\fs24 . Instead of relying on a single method, it first attempts to answer a query with a fast, pattern-based system. If the query is too complex, it intelligently escalates to the more powerful Text-to-SQL agent.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Text-to-SQL Agent (The "SQL Architect")
\f0\b0 : A 
\f1\b LangChain SQL Agent
\f0\b0  powered by a local 
\f1\b Ollama
\f0\b0  model (
\f2\b\fs26 codellama
\f0\b0\fs24 ). This agent is given a highly specific custom prompt and access to the database's enriched schema (including your descriptive comments), allowing it to write precise PostgreSQL queries for complex questions.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Vector Search (The "Researcher")
\f0\b0 : Uses a 
\f1\b Hugging Face Sentence Transformer
\f0\b0  model to convert the user's query into a vector embedding. It then queries a 
\f1\b Supabase pgvector
\f0\b0  database to find and retrieve relevant, unstructured documents for added context.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Narrative LLM (The "Reporter")
\f0\b0 : A fast, powerful 
\f1\b Groq API
\f0\b0  model (
\f1\b Llama3
\f0\b0 ). Its sole job is to synthesize the final answer. It receives the structured data from the SQL query and the unstructured context from the vector search and generates a final, credible, human-readable narrative.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Database (Supabase PostgreSQL)
\f0\b0 : Serves as a dual-purpose data store for both the structured, relational vessel data and the unstructured vector embeddings for semantic search.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 ## Data Flow: Anatomy of a Query\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
The application processes a user's question in a sophisticated, multi-stage pipeline to ensure both accuracy and contextual richness.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A user submits a natural language question (e.g., 
\f3\i "tell all you know about vessels type brig"
\f0\i0 ) to the 
\f4\fs26 POST /query
\f0\fs24  API endpoint in 
\f2\b\fs26 main.py
\f0\b0\fs24 .\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The server passes the query to the 
\f2\b\fs26 process_nl_query
\f0\b0\fs24  function.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The function first attempts a fast, 
\f1\b rule-based
\f0\b0  conversion to SQL.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The system checks the confidence of the rule-based result. If it's low, the 
\f1\b manual override
\f0\b0  invokes the 
\f2\b\fs26 codellama
\f1\fs24  SQL Agent
\f0\b0 .\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f2\b\fs26 codellama
\f1\fs24  agent
\f0\b0 , guided by its custom prompt and the database comments, generates and executes a precise PostgreSQL query.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In parallel, the user's query is sent to the 
\f1\b Vector Search
\f0\b0  component to find relevant documents from the Supabase vector store.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The final two pieces of information\'97the 
\f1\b structured data
\f0\b0  from the SQL query and the 
\f1\b unstructured context
\f0\b0  from the vector search\'97are sent to the 
\f1\b Groq Llama3
\f0\b0  model.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f1\b Narrative LLM
\f0\b0  synthesizes these inputs into a final, credible answer.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A complete JSON object containing the generated SQL, the raw data, and the final narrative is returned to the user's application.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
