\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 ## Deployment \uc0\u55357 \u56960 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
The application is self-contained and designed for straightforward deployment.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 ### Hugging Face Spaces\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
Hugging Face Spaces is an excellent platform for hosting demos.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Create a 
\f2\fs26 requirements.txt
\f1\fs24  file
\f0\b0 : From your active virtual environment, run 
\f4\fs26 pip freeze > requirements.txt
\f0\fs24 . This lists all necessary Python libraries.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rename 
\f2\fs26 main.py
\f1\fs24  to 
\f2\fs26 app.py
\f0\b0\fs24 : Hugging Face Spaces typically looks for a file named 
\f4\fs26 app.py
\f0\fs24  to run.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Upload Files
\f0\b0 : Upload your project to a new Space, ensuring your file structure is preserved (e.g., the 
\f4\fs26 app/services/
\f0\fs24  directory).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use Hugging Face Secrets
\f0\b0 : Do 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  upload your 
\f4\fs26 .env
\f0\fs24  file. Instead, go to your Space's "Settings" page and add your environment variables (like 
\f4\fs26 POSTGRES_USER
\f0\fs24 , 
\f4\fs26 GROQ_API_KEY
\f0\fs24 , etc.) as 
\f1\b Secrets
\f0\b0 . The application will be able to access them securely.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 ### Cloning for General Deployment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
To deploy the application on any server that runs Python:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Clone the Repository
\f0\b0 : 
\f4\fs26 git clone <your_repository_url>
\f0\fs24 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Set up Environment
\f0\b0 : Create a Python virtual environment and install the dependencies: 
\f4\fs26 pip install -r requirements.txt
\f0\fs24 .\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Configure
\f0\b0 : Create a 
\f4\fs26 .env
\f0\fs24  file in the root directory and add the required database and API key credentials.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Run
\f0\b0 : Start the application with 
\f4\fs26 python app.py
\f0\fs24 .\
}